I think this has varying levels of mystifying-ness. To others "posterior" is already mystifying enough. I think “a posteriori” is okay and so my okay-ness with MLE transfers over to M “a posteriori”. What about “mode of a joint density”, which is what it really is, and this has applications beyond finding modes of conditional distributions whose joint has an analytic form.

(I hope we can all agree it’s not as ambiguous as random effects or empirical Bayes!)

