Hi everyone,

I reckon a new version of CmdStan-dev was recently released, and I noted something odd. The fix we implemented (adding #define FUSION_MAX_VECTOR_SIZE 20 at the top of the term_grammar_def.hpp file) no longer works, because, according to the compiler, FUSION_MAX_VECTOR_SIZE is already defined in:

stan/lib/stan_math/lib/boost_1.58.0/boost/fusion/container/vector/limits.hpp.

The compiler's message appeared as a Warning, but then the two errors associated with the argument limit (see previous messages) showed up again.

I got everything running by editing limits.hpp and directly changing FUSION_MAX_VECTOR_SIZE. I wanted to share this updated fix. Also, any idea why redefining FUSION_MAX_VECTOR_SIZE became an issue?

