> sample space into sets then you can always construct a discrete
> probabilistic system implicitly by the mass function with takes
>
> p(x_{1}) = \mathbb{P} [ A_{1} ].
>
> Kind of like a singular marginalization from a continuous space
> into a discrete one.

Right.  I really do get all this now, I think.  What I was poining
out is that you are implicitly doing this when you construct the
sample space as a cross-prodcut of a discrete and continuous space.
Each discrete outcome corresponds to uncountably many points in the
sample space (though only one when you project down to its dimension).

- Bob

