The language of random variables is widely used in applied
stats papers and textbooks, so yes, it's important for classes.
Do you need it to do applied stats?  No!  Will it be confusing
to read the literature if you don't know what it is?  Yes!
It's what I found most confusing in the applied literature,
especially Bayesian stuff that conflates a ton of notation and
uses the language of random variables, like BDA.

- Bob

