From: u8aa9b8cc06fdc99c at groups.google.com (Bob Carpenter)
Date: Thu, 31 Mar 2016 00:12:18 +0000
Subject: buffering output [was [stan-users] RStan multiple parallel instances ...]
Message-ID: <mLRvfD8JRVU.8Qx2X4EzBwAJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-dev/c/mLRvfD8JRVU/m/8Qx2X4EzBwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Should we be thinking about some kind of buffering mechanism
for the output that doesn't involve files?  Network file
systems can have high latency, which would really benefit from
buffering if the output isn't needed online.

I'm thinking we could build that functionality into specialized
writer filters (basically writer classes that hold references to
other writers).

- Bob

